   "title": "Note: 1 - Refined shot + face crop",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 1 - Refined shot + face crop\n\n- **path:** the FaceRefine Plus output of the wide shot, i.e. step 2 of method B. The example is `method_b/refined_shot_A.mp4`.\n- **Face Select + Track Crop** detect the face and crop a square around it on every frame (crop_factor 2.0, 768 px).\n- **Image From Batch, image 1:** the frame to turn into the portrait. Pick one where the face is large, sharp, close to frontal and not mid-word. Look at the preview, then change `batch_index`.\n- **Image From Batch, image 2:** a second frame of the same shot, as an extra identity view.\n\nTip: in a shot where the subject walks toward the camera, the last frames have the largest face."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## 1 - Refined shot + face crop\n\n- **path:** the FaceRefine Plus output of the wide shot, i.e. step 2 of method B. The example is `method_b/refined_shot_A.mp4`.\n- **Face Select + Track Crop** detect the face and crop a square around it on every frame (crop_factor 2.0, 768 px).\n- **Image From Batch, image 1:** the frame to turn into the portrait. Pick one where the face is large, sharp, close to frontal and not mid-word. Look at the preview, then change `batch_index`.\n- **Image From Batch, image 2:** a second frame of the same shot, as an extra identity view.\n\nTip: in a shot where the subject walks toward the camera, the last frames have the largest face."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 304,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    570,
    40
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    420
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 7,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Note: 2 - Qwen Image 2.1: neutral portrait",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 2 - Qwen Image 2.1: the neutral portrait\n\nThe prompt turns image 1 into a reference portrait:\n- head and shoulders, front view;\n- neutral expression, mouth closed;\n- soft studio light, plain grey background.\n\nIt keeps the identity of images 1 and 2 (face shape, eyes, nose, lips, skin tone, hairstyle). Adapt `young Italian woman` to your subject.\n\n- euler / simple, 25 steps, cfg 1.0.\n- Make 2-3 seeds and keep the one that looks most like the refined shot. In the examples the pick was automatic: highest ArcFace similarity to the refined shot.\n\nUse Qwen Image Edit, not Flux Kontext / Klein-type editors: those change the person."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## 2 - Qwen Image 2.1: the neutral portrait\n\nThe prompt turns image 1 into a reference portrait:\n- head and shoulders, front view;\n- neutral expression, mouth closed;\n- soft studio light, plain grey background.\n\nIt keeps the identity of images 1 and 2 (face shape, eyes, nose, lips, skin tone, hairstyle). Adapt `young Italian woman` to your subject.\n\n- euler / simple, 25 steps, cfg 1.0.\n- Make 2-3 seeds and keep the one that looks most like the refined shot. In the examples the pick was automatic: highest ArcFace similarity to the refined shot.\n\nUse Qwen Image Edit, not Flux Kontext / Klein-type editors: those change the person."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 305,
